From 141d6103c9c29e7894cfe80b9345138747b1bca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darkmaniac7 <31073889+darkmaniac7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:41:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] firmware: push2, RAM release handler, primed alarm,
 fail-closed timeline

Run on one card on 2026-11-20 (about 500 shots). Marker
fw=lab-psr1-push2 (fw=lab-psr1-push2-debug). The lab's build differs
from this series only in how the unlock readback is arranged (patch
0007), so its checksum differs.

Release timing. With push1 the first alarm release of every boot came
9 to 10 us late and later shots 0 to 2 us; with push2 the first shot of
three fresh boots released at 0.
- The release handler is installed directly on the alarm IRQ with
  irq_set_exclusive_handler, highest priority, in SRAM
  (__not_in_flash_func); its body is inline register accesses only.
  Arming and cancel stay SDK calls.
- A throwaway alarm (pin already high-Z) runs before every shot;
  prime_at=<us> is printed; a priming alarm that never runs aborts.
- Core 1 feeds the watchdog with busy_wait_us: sleep_us added an alarm
  to the default pool every 500 us, whose IRQ runs on core 0 under spin
  locks with interrupts masked.
- No printf between the command and the end of the shot: the echo, WARN
  and FAIL lines are printed afterwards; i2c_bring_up stays quiet during
  a shot (the failure is in the step records).

Fail closed:
- The release alarm is armed by the assert step after PEX_RST is low,
  with interrupts off; an assert more than one write (47 us) late fails.
- Refused before any write: a VOUT step the setup write overwrites, and
  any PMBus write in flight across t = 0, counting 47 us per write and
  the queueing of back-to-back writes (td +30 with pw 36, for example:
  its restore queues to -40 us and runs past the release).
- Profile: capture refused when tainted (no reuse of an older capture);
  `u` forgets the capture; apply checked (the full profile's 0x31 write,
  which this controller refuses, excepted); restore only the registers
  the fast value touched, then read them back.
- The timeline stops at the first failed action; the stock rail is
  written while the card is still in reset when possible, then PEX_RST
  is released (via=abort); records only for the actions that ran.

SCL hold and dither:
- scl_hold(false) waits up to 200 us for SCL to read high (else the step
  fails); after a hold from the release the stock VOUT 0x7E runs 200 us
  after the hold and retries for up to 500 us; the profile restore waits
  200 us after any hold; hold_at=post gets a WARN line.
- Dither pw floor 47 us; writes scheduled closer than 47 us get a WARN.
- PEX_RST and SCL: output value set before the direction.

Builds for pico2_w (RP2350A and RP2350B) and pico2, normal and debug,
with no warnings.
